{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1057793-the-makara-issue-and-in-someway-eshmaki","id":1057793,"title":"The Makara issue (and in someway Eshmaki)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-03T15:53:21-08:00","id":1057793,"title":"The Makara issue (and in someway Eshmaki)","content":"Hello! I am new to the forums and to the CoD (played WoD a long time ago)<br /> <br /> Ok, my problem is that i cant take a grip with the Makara family.<br /> Anakins represent the fear of hopelessness, Namtaru represent the fear of revulsion, Ugallu represent the fear of exposure. They represent the result of the fear, someone that have stage panic can fit in the fear of exposure. In other words, they represent the felling that you have after facing a fear.<br /> Eshmaki represent the fear of darkness, but what exactly is the fear of darkness? Well, to me is the fear of the unknown. Ok, supposing that this is true let's go to Makara.<br /> Makara is the fear of the depths... Ok, so what exactly is the fear of the depths? Is the fear of unknown? Well, i said that Eshmaki handle this. It's the fear of &quot;transgressing a point and knowing that you can't return? Well, this is hopelessness and to this we have the Anakin. So what i should expect from a Makara?<br /> The point here is that with Anakins,Namtarus and Ugallus we have a pattern, they represent the repulsing felling of a fear, don't matter what this fear really is. What is repulsive to one people could be normal to another. But Makaras and Eshmakis represent a something more concrete and not the resulting felling, and can pull something from Eshmakis but with the Makaras i an having a hard time.<br /> The concept of monsters from the ocean don't fit with the others families. You can have a a crepping Ugallu, a tiny Anakin and to me Jason it's a Eshmaki even if everyone sees him.<br /> Well, my english is not good so i hope you understand my question. I want to understand the Makaras and the Eshmakis in the same way i understand the others.<br /> <br /> TY<br /> <br /> David Paiva","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:01:53-08:00","id":1057796,"title":"","content":"My personal interpretation is that the Eshmaki are the fears of the things which hide in the darkness and the unknown, while the Makara are the fears of the enormity and unknowability of the world. Makara are the ocean which can never be explored, the library too big to find that secret you need and the cold, airless vacuum of space, with the monsters as extensions of their environments. The Eshmaki are the thing which you know are there and which you can hear breathing behind you, beneath the bed, beyond the firelight. <br /> <br /> As I say, though, that's just my interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:04:28-08:00","id":1057799,"title":"","content":"So Eshmaki is the fear of something lurking you? And then Makara would be the real fear of the unknown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:04:48-08:00","id":1057800,"title":"","content":"While I've always felt a particular connection with other redheads (read: Ariel) and so immediately made a literal mermaid for the Ready-Made PCs Makara, they don't have to be literal mermaids. It's also addiction. Idk why, but I'm also suddenly thinking of the quotes from &quot;The Prestige&quot; about obsession.<br /> <br /> Those are my totally unorganized thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:06:32-08:00","id":1057801,"title":"","content":"Makara are the fear of Lovecraft's work, of an uncaring universe too big to face, of unknowable, monstrous mystery, while Eshmaki are that most primitive of fears: The fear of the shapeless, formless monster out there in the dark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:07:28-08:00","id":1057803,"title":"","content":"Hum... A pure light flying Makara would be something really weird, lol.<br /> Maybe it wouldn't<br /> have a fixed form so you don't know what the hell is this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:08:11-08:00","id":1057804,"title":"","content":"Hum... I just fell that this thing of too big to face it's a Anakin thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:08:45-08:00","id":1057806,"title":"","content":"Eshmaki would be the monster under the bed, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:11:18-08:00","id":1057807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1057793-the-makara-issue-and-in-someway-eshmaki?p=1057800#post1057800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I've always felt a particular connection with other redheads (read: Ariel) and so immediately made a literal mermaid for the Ready-Made PCs Makara, they don't have to be literal mermaids. It's also addiction. Idk why, but I'm also suddenly thinking of the quotes from &quot;The Prestige&quot; about obsession.<br /> <br /> Those are my totally unorganized thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved the mermaid and the other characters btw","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:20:36-08:00","id":1057815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1057793-the-makara-issue-and-in-someway-eshmaki?p=1057807#post1057807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I loved the mermaid and the other characters btw</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I really appreciate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:49:29-08:00","id":1057831,"title":"","content":"A thing to understand in my mind is that it isn't like the archetypes of each family don't contain any overlap. I mean let's face Anakim are hopelessness and it's not hard to imagine any of the other families inflicting hopelessness on the target.<br /> <br /> The way I play it, the Eshmaki are your primal fear of the unknown. You know something is out there, but not specifically what it is, or where it is or what it wants.<br /> <br /> The Makara have traces of this, but it isn't the same. The Makara I view as a fear of potential. The ocean isn't going to kill you, but it could. So you know the threat, unlike an Eshmaki where all you know is that there is a threat, or an Anakim where knowing about the threat is useless as soon as it has become a threat. The Makara are fears that can be, will the ship sink, will the ladder break, did that camera get enough view of me to identify me in that murder I committed. <br /> <br /> If the Eshmaki can be represented by a fear of the future, then I'd say the Makara are a fear of the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:42:20-08:00","id":1057891,"title":"","content":"The Eshmaki are the fear that there's something <i>behind</i>.<br /> <br /> Whether that's behind the door, behind the mask, behind <i>you</i>, or some more particular screening method, the Lurkers are the fear of the hidden.<br /> <br /> Though they conceptuallu neighbor the drowning despair of the Anakim and the endless vistas of the Ugallu, a Makara dwells within the fear that you are surrounded, whether literally or figuratively, by a species/medium to which your capacity to resist is insufficient.<br /> <br /> The Giant's strike can be evaded for a time and the Raptor can be staved off by temporary cover, but the Nightmares of the Depths do not engage in something so base as a <i>pursuit</i> \u2014 the moment of terror they embody resonates within the very belly of the Leviathan itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T20:17:36-08:00","id":1057910,"title":"","content":"More shortly; if you can describe something as <i>drowning</i>, whether literally or metaphorically, it's probably Makara.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:05:15-08:00","id":1058203,"title":"","content":"I mostly see the Fear of the Dephts as encompassing the fears of being deceived by appearances, of being lost, of being in a hostile environment, of caving under pressure. At the same time the fears of what is lying beneath the surface and of finding oneself there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:17:23-08:00","id":1058206,"title":"","content":"Makara also embody a fear of hidden knowledge and lost lore: &quot;The terrible truth&quot; is a Makara fear (the Ugallu too, but it's more &quot;<i>Your </i>terrible truth&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T21:11:44-08:00","id":1058287,"title":"","content":"Anakim are the fear of a foe you <u><i><b>cannot defeat</b></i></u>; someone/something that can crush you without a second thought.<br /> Makara are the fear of being <u><i><b>out of your element</b></i></u>, literally or figuratively; being in a place or set of circumstances that you are simply not built to survive in.<br /> Eshmaki are the fear of an <u><i><b>unexpected danger</b></i></u>; it's out there, and you might even KNOW it's out there, but you don't know for sure where or when the threat is going to strike.<br /> Ugallu are the fear of having <u><i><b>no where to hide</b></i></u>; you are exposed, literally or figuratively, and there is nothing you can do about it.<br /> \u200bNamtaru are the fear of <u><i><b>being alone and unwanted</b></i></u>; it will make you ugly, like it is ugly.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr at least those are my understandings; I don't actually have the book. I still can't figure out why Eshmaki can breath fire, when blending into the shadows makes <u><i><b>WAY</b></i></u> more sense for <u><i><b>LURKERS</b></i></u>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 03-05-2017, 06:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T06:18:29-08:00","id":1058380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>draxdeveloper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1057793-the-makara-issue-and-in-someway-eshmaki#post1057793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello! I am new to the forums and to the CoD (played WoD a long time ago)<br /> <br /> Ok, my problem is that i cant take a grip with the Makara family.<br /> Anakins represent the fear of hopelessness, Namtaru represent the fear of revulsion, Ugallu represent the fear of exposure. They represent the result of the fear, someone that have stage panic can fit in the fear of exposure. In other words, they represent the felling that you have after facing a fear.<br /> Eshmaki represent the fear of darkness, but what exactly is the fear of darkness? Well, to me is the fear of the unknown. Ok, supposing that this is true let's go to Makara.<br /> Makara is the fear of the depths... Ok, so what exactly is the fear of the depths? Is the fear of unknown? Well, i said that Eshmaki handle this. It's the fear of &quot;transgressing a point and knowing that you can't return? Well, this is hopelessness and to this we have the Anakin. So what i should expect from a Makara?<br /> The point here is that with Anakins,Namtarus and Ugallus we have a pattern, they represent the repulsing felling of a fear, don't matter what this fear really is. What is repulsive to one people could be normal to another. But Makaras and Eshmakis represent a something more concrete and not the resulting felling, and can pull something from Eshmakis but with the Makaras i an having a hard time.<br /> The concept of monsters from the ocean don't fit with the others families. You can have a a crepping Ugallu, a tiny Anakin and to me Jason it's a Eshmaki even if everyone sees him.<br /> Well, my english is not good so i hope you understand my question. I want to understand the Makaras and the Eshmakis in the same way i understand the others.<br /> <br /> TY<br /> <br /> David Paiva</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Makara's depths can be literal, or metaphorical. Yeah, lots of people fear drowning; but how often are you really at risk of being submerged until death? The depths they represent could be portrayed through the use of <b>politics</b>, <i>corruption</i>, <u>financial debt</u>, <b>mysteries</b>, <i>conspiracies</i>, <u>madness</u>, <b>emotions</b>, <i>faith,</i> or <u>lies.</u> Anything that would threaten those who immerse themselves too deeply within it are viable tools for a terror of the deep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-05-2017, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:59:24-08:00","id":1058584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>draxdeveloper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1057793-the-makara-issue-and-in-someway-eshmaki?p=1057804#post1057804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hum... I just fell that this thing of too big to face it's a Anakin thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just as I described with the Makara, any of these families can either be taken literally, or portrayed from a metaphorical standpoint. Often, if you use the metaphorical version, it opens up a huge variety of different types of monsters from each respective family.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anakim are the fear of powerlessness. They're not so much the creature who starts smashing everything in sight, but rather they are the kind who stand in front of an entire squad of hunters and says <b>&quot;You know what? I'll be a good sport and give you the first blow!&quot;</b> as they stand there with arms lowered to their sides. Anakim are the unstoppable, the uncontrollable. They are chaos, they are a force of nature, they are the riddle you can't crack, the chains you can't remove, they stand above the law. They give their victims a 10 minute head start, because they know it won't make a difference. The Anakim always get what they want, you can not stop them.<i> That's the horror they represent.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Remember:</b> the prophecy of Ragnarok says that Giants are destined to claim victory. Our so called gods (i.e 'Heroes') die brutally at their hands. And when their work is finished, the only thing we can do is try to rebuild what was lost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1057793-the-makara-issue-and-in-someway-eshmaki?p=1058287#post1058287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOr at least those are my understandings; I don't actually have the book. I still can't figure out why Eshmaki can breath fire, when blending into the shadows makes <u><i><b>WAY</b></i></u> more sense for <u><i><b>LURKERS</b></i></u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eshmaki are the fear of destruction, and one possible monster for them is that of the dragon. The creature who swoops down and starts burning everything around them until the whole city lies in flames.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-05-2017, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:17:02-08:00","id":1058601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1057793-the-makara-issue-and-in-someway-eshmaki?p=1058287#post1058287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anakim are the fear of a foe you <u><i><b>cannot defeat</b></i></u>; someone/something that can crush you without a second thought.<br /> Makara are the fear of being <u><i><b>out of your element</b></i></u>, literally or figuratively; being in a place or set of circumstances that you are simply not built to survive in.<br /> Eshmaki are the fear of an <u><i><b>unexpected danger</b></i></u>; it's out there, and you might even KNOW it's out there, but you don't know for sure where or when the threat is going to strike.<br /> Ugallu are the fear of having <u><i><b>no where to hide</b></i></u>; you are exposed, literally or figuratively, and there is nothing you can do about it.<br /> \u200bNamtaru are the fear of <u><i><b>being alone and unwanted</b></i></u>; it will make you ugly, like it is ugly.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr at least those are my understandings; I don't actually have the book. I still can't figure out why Eshmaki can breath fire, when blending into the shadows makes <u><i><b>WAY</b></i></u> more sense for <u><i><b>LURKERS</b></i></u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because in the old days when fire wasn't taken for granted, being hit by a huge glob of it was one hell of a surprise. It is still now, since most people don't really expect fire to attack them. It's why so many people throw lit cigars in the forest, and leave their stoves open and burning. That, and the blinding light generated by fire can blind people just as much as darkness can. Hiding in plain sight and daylight is counter-intuitive, but if anyone tries that with success it's going to be the Lurkers. <br /> <br /> Gorgons can emerge from the shadows because that's where the unloved, unwanted, and unbidden are shunted off and forgotten. They crawl out of the same place that people dare not to look at, lest they be consumed by it. This isn't a surprise attack. People feel terror while expecting the darkness to contain something nasty. So the Gorgons oblige, and realize that terror into a horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T05:37:31-08:00","id":1060033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1057793-the-makara-issue-and-in-someway-eshmaki?p=1058287#post1058287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eshmaki are the fear of an <u><i><b>unexpected danger</b></i></u>; it's out there, and you might even KNOW it's out there, but you don't know for sure where or when the threat is going to strike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you make an argument for an Eshmaki horror being a living-natural-disaster-type, then? After all, for all that you hear about hurricanes and tsunamis and so on, no-one really expects it to happen to them. That might just be a thing over here in the 'enlightened and indolent West', but still...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T20:56:04-07:00","id":1061719,"title":"","content":"Ironically, most sea monsters would be Eshmaki:<br /> <br /> It's down there in the water. Somewhere.<br /> You can't see the bottom.<br /> Was that a tickle against your toes?<br /> <i>Oh shit, oh shit, oh shit.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T21:24:56-07:00","id":1061724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1057793-the-makara-issue-and-in-someway-eshmaki?p=1061719#post1061719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically, most sea monsters would be Eshmaki:<br /> <br /> It's down there in the water. Somewhere.<br /> You can't see the bottom.<br /> Was that a tickle against your toes?<br /> <i>Oh shit, oh shit, oh shit.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>that's why i said it's kind of a issue. Since it's not really intuitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}